Do not infer the first argument of a ``classmethod`` defined outside a class
body, such as in a factory function or at module level, as the enclosing
function or module. There is no class to bind it to there, so ``cls`` is now
inferred as ``Uninferable``. This removes ``no-member`` and
``too-many-function-args`` false positives reported by pylint on such code.

Refs #3462
Closes pylint-dev/pylint#7487
